3) local vs global constants when using the includeLuaFile() feature of RailCOMPLETE: Please try to formulate this in an instructive manner in the Skills document to be made:



When a script file declares a global Lua identifier (such as: _VERSION_ = "v1.2") and thereafter makes a reference to libraries of functions with the includeLuaFile() API call from RailCOMPLETE, then the outermost (calling) sandbox creates a child  sandbox per include file and passes all global constants to each child sandbox. In the child sandbox, the globally inherited constant may be used as-is or may be overridden by an assignment to that identifier (since Lua does not have protected constants, it is just a variable that you don't intend to change, normally), or it may be may replaced by a local declaration using the same identifier name - whereupon the call to a next level child sandboxed includeLuaFile() would NOT inherited neither the top-level version or the locally declared identifer on the same name.



---GLOBAL CONSTANTS---



---INCLUDES---

local lib1 = includeLuaFile("Lua\\Functions\\lib1.lua")

local lib2 = includeLuaFile("Lua\\Functions\\lib2.lua")

local VA = includeLuaFile("Lua\\Functions\\lib2_VA.lua")



---LOCAL CONSTANTS---

local _USAGE_ = "To this, then do that...blah, blah, blah."





